  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 406.05 Identification of Other Jurisdictional Areas",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 406.05 Identification of Other Jurisdictional Areas. Jurisdictional areas not subject to delineation as described in Env-Wt 406.01, Env-Wt 406.02, or Env-Wt 406.04 shall be identified as described below, as applicable:\n\n(a) Any features subject to Env-Wt 600 shall be delineated based on their definitions;\n\n(b) Surface water bodies such as lakes and ponds shall be delineated to the limit of the bank and include the normal high water line; and\n\n(c) For any project in a prime wetlands or a duly-established 100-foot buffer for which a delineation has been submitted to the department pursuant to Env-Wt 703, the delineation identified in Env-Wt 703.06 shall be used.\n\nSource. #12804, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt400.html"
